                   "max_tokens_with_reasoning":  {
                                                     "question":  "What do the official docs say about max_tokens / completion tokens with reasoning (thinking mode)?",
                                                     "finding":  "PARTIAL. The Chat Completions API reference defines max_tokens as the maximum number of tokens that can be generated in the chat completion, with total input+generated tokens limited by context length, and points to the Models \u0026 Pricing page for the value range and default. The Models \u0026 Pricing page lists MAX OUTPUT MAXIMUM: 384K but no default value, and neither the Thinking Mode guide nor the Token Usage guide states that reasoning tokens count toward max_tokens. No current official statement was found that reasoning tokens are included in max_tokens or completion_tokens (such a statement existed in earlier DeepSeek R1-era docs, but the current pages do not contain it).",
                                                     "evidence":  [
                                                                      {
                                                                          "lang":  "en",
                                                                          "page_file":  "deepseek-create-chat-completion-en.html",
